  checker (station_goal_checker, nav2_params.yaml), and with two checkers an empty goal_checker_id is refused
  ("FollowPath called with goal_checker name ... which does not exist"). (2) BackUp is removed from RecoveryActions
  (Alex, 19 Nov 2026: no general reversing recovery; D-19, rear sectors masked). (3) ClearEntireCostmap ->
  ClearCostmapAroundRobot (bounded, reset_distance 3.0 m global / 1.5 m local) in all four places (platform-sw#124
  D-19 audit, #92): stock wipes the WHOLE costmap unconditionally on every planner/controller failure and every
  round-robin cycle, erasing real, currently-correct obstacle data anywhere else on the map. (4) A named
  Wait(2.0s) inserted immediately before each inline bounded clear (WaitBeforeClear-GlobalContext,
  WaitBeforeClear-LocalContext): RecoveryTracker matches the bare node name "Wait" to count a recovery attempt
  (same name the outer round-robin's genuine Wait(5.0) below uses) - naming these keeps an ordinary inline clear
  from being miscounted as a real escalated recovery. (5) FollowPath names
  progress_checker_id="progress_checker" (PROPOSED, 23 Nov 2026, platform-sw #192): controller_server has a second
  progress checker (station_progress_checker) and refuses an empty progress_checker_id the same way. The checker this
  tree uses is the one it used before. Every other line is the stock tree.
